envelope: 1
uuid: nexus-export-schema-injection
type: schema
id: injection
context: >-
  copilot/schemas — sovereign local copy. Origin: lib/node-schemas/schema.injection (shared
  canonical version, may have moved on independently since this copy was made — sovereignty
  means copilot does not depend on it at runtime, not that the two can never drift). This is
  also the ONLY real construction site (copilot/tool-runtime.js), so this sovereign copy is
  the origin, not a downstream copy of behavior defined elsewhere.
intent: null
summary: null
system: copilot
tags: []
exported_at: 1789269378487
source: nexus.lib.node-export
payload:
  status: REAL
  source: >-
    One real, exact construction site, checked directly: copilot/tool-runtime.js's makeNcpCallModel's
    inner callModel — the exact function v0.39.122 ("mountain" fix) patched. Every call computes
    primed = _isFreshlyPrimed(opts.provider), then either reuses convo alone (primed) or builds
    fullPrompt = [system, _toolInstructions(scoped, {guide:true}), convo].join('\n\n') (not primed) —
    the real, single place text gets prepended to an outbound NCP dispatch. copilot/tool-runtime.js's
    makeOllamaCallModel was checked and excluded: ollama-bridge's /api/chat takes a native `tools`
    param (toolSchemas passed straight through to dispatch()), so that path never text-injects a tool
    guide at all — there is no second real injection site to fold in.
  fields:
    provider:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: >-
        real target provider this dispatch iteration resolved to — opts.provider as passed into
        makeNcpCallModel's callModel; 'auto' or unresolved is recorded as-is, never guessed
    primed:
      type: boolean
      required: true
      description: >-
        real _isFreshlyPrimed(provider) result for this call — true means convo alone was sent,
        false means system + tool guide were rebuilt and prepended
    injectedSystemPrompt:
      type: boolean
      required: true
      description: 'real: whether `system` (messages.find(role===''system'').content) was included this call — always equal to !primed'
    injectedToolGuide:
      type: boolean
      required: true
      description: >-
        real: whether _toolInstructions(scoped, {guide:true}) was included this call — recorded as
        its own field, not folded into injectedSystemPrompt, because the two were two independently-
        built, previously-uncoordinated pieces (the exact stacking cause of the v0.39.122 bug) — kept
        distinguishable in case they diverge again
    toolCount:
      type: number
      required: true
      description: real scoped.length — the number of tools actually offered this call, after opts.toolScope narrowing
    promptLength:
      type: number
      required: true
      description: >-
        real fullPrompt.length actually sent this call — the exact figure the mountain bug was
        measured in (61,809 vs 16,039 chars for the duplicated-guide case)
    idleMsThreshold:
      type: number
      required: true
      description: >-
        real PROVIDER_IDLE_MS constant used for this decision (120000, matches clear-glass/src/
        providers/host.js's own IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS) — recorded so the record explains its own threshold
        without needing the source read
    msSinceLastPrimed:
      type: number
      required: false
      description: >-
        real (Date.now() - _lastPrimedAt.get(provider)) at decision time — the actual evidence behind
        primed; absent when provider was never primed before (map had no entry)
